<title>AUSTRALIA: PBL year net profit jumps.</title>
<headline>PBL year net profit jumps.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-09-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		   260.82 vs 219.70</p>
<p>    Net				    225.39 vs 149.94</p>
<p>    Abnormal		     profit 52.71 vs nil</p>
<p>    Final dividend (cents)	     8.00 vs 7.00</p>
<p>NOTE: Publishing and Broadcasting Ltd is a television network operator and magazine publisher whose major shareholder is interest's associated with businessman Kerry Packer.  </p>
<p>    Total dividend (cents)	    15.00 vs 14.00</p>
<p>    Sales (billion)			1.13 vs 0.93</p>
<p>    Other income			 202.78 vs 25.57</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			   55.00 vs 36.91</p>
<p>Dividend is 100 percent franked</p>
<p>Pay date November 15</p>
<p>Reg date October 31</p>
<p>    Tax				     85.52 vs 69.89</p>
<p>    Interest				61.72 vs 46.63</p>
<p>    Depreciation			  20.04 vs 17.49</p>
<p>    Minorities		    charge 2.62 vs credit 0.12</p>
<p>NOTE: Comparative figures for the previous year contain 12 months results for Nine Network but only eight months for ACP, the magazine division. When restated as 12 months figures, revenue at A$1.095 billion is 4.0 percent higher than the previous corresponding period, earnings before interest, tax and abnormals are 4.7 percent higher at A$311.1 million and earnings before interest and tax but after abnormals are 22.5 percent higher at A$297.0 million.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373 1800</p>
</text>
